{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1020104-hurt-locker-on-developing-merit-templates","id":1020104,"title":"[Hurt Locker] On Developing Merit Templates","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-20T18:42:31-08:00","id":1020104,"title":"[Hurt Locker] On Developing Merit Templates","content":"Now that we've seen them done up properly, anyone out there have any thoughts on how to develop new ones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T18:57:55-08:00","id":1020118,"title":"","content":"Think of an overarching theme for the template, and add in a mechanic that is prevelent throughout (such as the Memory of the Dreamers, or The Lost Boys' Serum deprivation). Make merits that play with this mechanic, such as making it easier to utilize certain aspects of it or offering alternative methods for gaining it as a resource. Make potent abilities have drawbacks or limitations that make them situational. Remember that for all these offer, this is pretty much a normal human with an overarching supernatural aspect now.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm trying to make a version of the Kamen Rider series with the aforementioned method. Do note, though, that what i've mentioned above is wildly minimalistic and probably not how to actually make such a template properly. Also I am tired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T22:02:59-08:00","id":1020183,"title":"","content":"And here I am, trying to cook up something that'd replicate the Persona Users from the Persona series (look my profile pic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T00:00:07-08:00","id":1020206,"title":"","content":"Heh, I was planning on doing Persona users as a merit template as well. Was going to have the inital benefit allow the user to interact with Goetia in twilight as if they were solid and you stat up a goetia which acts as your Persona. You can then get merits which give you resistance to attacks of the influences of your Persona, merits which decrease the penalties for interacting with Goetic ephemeral, for using the influences of your Persona, and for sending your Persona out of your body in twilight manifestation to battle against geotia. Abilities would function abit differently when you're in the Astral because you'd actually be summoning a solid Persona rather than projecting a twilight one for example.<br /> <br /> Then again, I also considered characters possibly having a Persona for each set of social merits you possess like Retainers/Status/Allies, where it's power is limited by the highest number of dots you have in a merit that represents that groups social-link. But that got complicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T01:25:33-08:00","id":1020224,"title":"","content":"For me, Kamen Riders would either fit as a Hunter splat or as a Merit Template. Both have merits, pun not intended, but considering how the more recent Rider series go for the heroes having as a great deal of gear and a great many forms (toy sales and all), it makes sense to go with a merit style.<br /> <br /> In terms of merits, most of them would apply only to the Rider Form, which itself would be a form of armor that would be activatable (possibly by a point of willpower). Once activated, it'd have a number of base abilities. Naturally, it'd have a base armor bonus against both firearms and melee, and come with a single merit dot to be spent to reflect the base form's natural capabilities. This could be a weapon, a vehicle (motorcycles preferred) or perhaps it naturally has an equipment bonus for certain tasks.<br /> <br /> The merits for the form would include weapons of varying types (ones with minor bonuses compared to normal ones), vehicles of unusual capability, and for various temporary powers. Naturally, purchases would be limited by the number of Merit dots you have (though limited to the number of dots, some multiple of them or simply limited to purchases of a certain level, I'm not sure). There could also be the merit Extant Form; this would basically be an alternate form the Rider could take with a point of willpower (possibly; working on whether I should include a resource mechanic to this), and it would include one/some of the aforementioned merits, depending on how many dots invested into the new form. Merits taken with Extant Form in mind cost less in return for requiring the willpower/resource point to access them, but the player could potentially purchase it for their base form in turn. This could also allow for more diversity for the forms...but I'd need to figure out a way to balance that.<br /> <br /> I'm also thinking of a Limit Break merit/ability, one that allows the Rider to have more points in a designated Attribute for a willpower/resource point, taking it above human normal, but for reach turn it's active it inflicts a Lethal damage to the user (to reflect how the body REALLY doesn't like being pushed too far). This would be useful for finishing moves, or simply inflicting a massive amount of damage, but it could also be used for other things. For example, a high Wits and or Composure score would be great for perception roles, or Stamina could be used to give health dots that would save a rider from a particularly damaging blow. It could even be used as a temporary source of Willpower, a heroic second wind. Of course, after the limit break there'd be some kind of penalty in turn (as noted, pushing the human body past its limits isn't healthy), to help limit the abuse of it.<br /> <br /> Another aspect is a Condition that Riders get for using the Limit Break or a potent Extant Form too much; in certain series <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Blade, OOO, Gaim, Gills, possibly others I'm unaware of </div></div> </div> </div>, the main hero using their super form (or even the nature of the armor itself) too much causes them to become the the very beings they are fighting against, usually as an end of the series twist. This results in more power to them, but at the cost of their humanity, and it isn't without mental strife among them and their allies. I think it'd be an interesting thing to balance out for players and their characters especially since in the series certain characters end up better than others in this state. Perhaps every use of a Limit Break/Potent Extant Form requires a roll based on your Merit's dots; each success advances you along the chain of mutation from Human to Other. On the one hand, you're notably less human, but on the other you start gaining a resistance trait to other supernatural powers, and you could potentially have other benefits. Do you use more power at the chance of becoming something other, with a very hard road to become completely human, or become a creature with great power but little to no humanity left? Or do you strive to go somewhere between both, a heroic monster that hunts their own?<br /> <br /> You can see why I'm having a dificult time deciding on whether this should be for a Hunter conspiracy or a Merit Template.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T07:21:25-08:00","id":1020387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1020104-hurt-locker-on-developing-merit-templates?p=1020206#post1020206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again, I also considered characters possibly having a Persona for each set of social merits you possess like Retainers/Status/Allies, where it's power is limited by the highest number of dots you have in a merit that represents that groups social-link. But that got complicated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Start with a personal Persona/Goetia, then allow Social-based ones as a descendant merit?<br /> <br /> What's the power scale, here? Because a simple method might be using Mage's Sympathy rules (regarding Connection/Withstand strength) as the Rank or Effective Rank of that Persona/Goetia (so a mere Rank 1 for a casual/tenuous connection, up to Rank 3 for deeply intimate ones).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}